[{"id":126066,"sender_id":11,"sender_full_name":"Urs","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/b00d1ee17463af676c78974439b92471?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/2-Latest-Changes/topic/manifold.20structure.20of.20mapping.20spaces/near/126066\">#30</a> The way the intro and bulk of this entry is worded (going back all the way to <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/revision/manifold+structure+of+mapping+spaces/1\">revision 1</a> by Andrew Stacey in 2010) gives the impression that compactness of the domain is generally necessary for the smooth mapping space to be Fréchet. (It doesn’t actually ever say this explicitly, but it’s hard not to read it that way.)</p>\n<p>But this seems far from true. I haven’t found a reference yet for the fully general case, but I added a subsection <em>Properties – Fréchet Lie group structure</em> (now <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/manifold+structure+of+mapping+spaces#FrechetLieGroupStructure\">here</a>) which recalls the statement for Lie group targets. Currently it reads as follows:</p>\n<hr>\n<p>Consider:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">G</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">G</span></span></span></span> a Milnor-regular <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/Fr%C3%A9chet%20Lie%20group\">Fréchet Lie group</a>, such as a finite-<a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/dimension%20of%20a%20manifold\">dimensional</a> <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/Lie%20group\">Lie group</a> or a <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/Banach%20manifold\">Banach manifold</a> <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/Lie%20group\">Lie group</a>,</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"double-struck\">R</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo>×</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">M = \\mathbb{R}^n \\times K</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.109em;\">M</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.7722em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathbb\">R</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.6644em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">n</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">×</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0715em;\">K</span></span></span></span> the <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/smooth%20manifold\">smooth</a> <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/product%20manifold\">product manifold</a> of a <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/Cartesian%20space\">Cartesian space</a> with any <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/smooth%20manifold\">smooth manifold</a> (finite <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/dimension%20of%20a%20manifold\">dimensional</a>).</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>\\begin{proposition}</p>\n<ul>\n<li>If <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">K</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0715em;\">K</span></span></span></span> is <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/compact%20topological%20space\">compact</a> </li>\n</ul>\n<p>or</p>\n<ul>\n<li>if <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">G</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">G</span></span></span></span> is a <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/vector%20space\">vector</a> <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/Fr%C3%A9chet%20space\">Fréchet space</a> (regarded as an <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/abelian%20group\">abelian</a> <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/Fr%C3%A9chet%20Lie%20group\">Fréchet Lie group</a>),</li>\n</ul>\n<p>then <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∞</mi></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">C^\\infty(M,G)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0715em;\">C</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.6644em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">∞</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.109em;\">M</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">G</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span> with <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/compact-open%20topology\">compact-open topology</a> and pointwise product is a Milnor-regular <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/Fr%C3%A9chet%20Lie%20group\">Fréchet Lie group</a>, locally modeled on <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∞</mi></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"fraktur\">g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">C^\\infty(M,\\mathfrak{g})</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0715em;\">C</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.6644em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">∞</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.109em;\">M</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathfrak\">g</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span>.</p>\n<p>\\end{proposition}</p>\n<p>(<a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/manifold+structure+of+mapping+spaces#NeebWagemann2008\">Neeb &amp; Wagemann 2008 Cor. II.8 &amp; Prop. I.2(1)</a>)</p>\n<hr>\n<p>I also added a warning editorial remark in the intro of the entry, where the impression first arises that compactness is necessary. But eventually we should remove that warning and instead reword the introduction (and the following text) to give a clearer picture right away.</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/revision/diff/manifold+structure+of+mapping+spaces/23\">diff</a>, <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/revision/manifold+structure+of+mapping+spaces/23\">v23</a>, <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/manifold+structure+of+mapping+spaces\">current</a></p>","timestamp":1789910335,"subject":"manifold structure of mapping spaces","stream_id":2,"display_recipient":"Latest Changes","reactions":[]},{"id":126067,"sender_id":11,"sender_full_name":"Urs","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/b00d1ee17463af676c78974439b92471?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/2-Latest-Changes/topic/manifold.20structure.20of.20mapping.20spaces/near/126067\">#31</a> Added pointers to Michor’s work on the issue:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/Peter%20W.%20Michor\">Peter W. Michor</a>: <em>Manifolds of Differentiable Mappings</em>, Shiva Publishing (1980) [<a href=\"http://www.mat.univie.ac.at/~michor/manifolds_of_differentiable_mappings.pdf\">pdf</a>, <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/Michor-MdM1980.pdf%3Afile\">Michor-MdM1980.pdf:file</a>]</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/Peter%20W.%20Michor\">Peter W. Michor</a>: <em>Manifolds of mappings and shapes</em>, in: Lizhen Ji, Frans Oort, <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/Shing-Tung%20Yau\">Shing-Tung Yau</a> (eds.): <em>The legacy of Bernhard Riemann after one hundred and fifty years</em>, ALM <strong>35</strong>, International Press Boston (2016) 459–486 [<a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/1505.02359\">arXiv:1505.02359 math.DG</a>]</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/Peter%20W.%20Michor\">Peter W. Michor</a>: <em>Manifolds of mappings for continuum mechanics</em>, in: Reuven Segev, Marcelo Epstein (eds).: <em>Geometric Continuum Mechanics</em>, Advances in Continuum Mechanics <strong>42</strong>, Birkhäuser (2020) 3–75 [<a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-030-42683-5_1\">doi:10.1007/978-3-030-42683-5_1</a>, <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/1909.00445\">arXiv:1909.00445 math.DG</a>]</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/Andreas%20Kriegl\">Andreas Kriegl</a>, <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/Peter%20Michor\">Peter Michor</a>: <em><a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/The%20Convenient%20Setting%20of%20Global%20Analysis\">The Convenient Setting of Global Analysis</a></em>: Mathematical Surveys and Monographs <strong>53</strong>, American Mathematical Society (1997) [ISBN: 978-0-8218-0780-4, <a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1090/surv/053\">doi:10.1090/surv/053</a>, <a href=\"https://bookstore.ams.org/surv-53\">ams:surv-53</a>, <a href=\"https://www.mat.univie.ac.at/~michor/apbookh-ams.pdf\">pdf</a>]</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>(the last one (only) was cited all along from the entry’s bulk text, but without the actual bibdata provided).</p>\n<p>From the results there, it seems that the statement that <em>is</em> true is something like this:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>For non-compact domain, a Fréchet manifold structure still exists, but its charts are not the ones you would expect to be working with.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/revision/diff/manifold+structure+of+mapping+spaces/24\">diff</a>, <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/revision/manifold+structure+of+mapping+spaces/24\">v24</a>, <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/manifold+structure+of+mapping+spaces\">current</a></p>","timestamp":1789920144,"subject":"manifold structure of mapping spaces","stream_id":2,"display_recipient":"Latest Changes","reactions":[]}]